{"authoredAt":"2026-08-24T16:16:49.939Z","conclusion":"findings","findings":[{"category":"missing","desc":"doc-promise-undelivered: docs/host-run-usage.md:515-516 and docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md:268-270 promise immediate erasure of prompt, capability, and one-shot environment after failed launch, claim, or startup. In packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts:1988-2021, the worker claims the run and can fail assertManagedReviewScratchExecution before entering the one-shot-input try/finally at lines 2025-2053. Its writeTerminal path at lines 1553-1613 cleans the external Claude prompt and detached scratch but does not unlink the durable capability, prompt, or environment files. Diagnostics and GC then classify those inputs as present and retain the run at lines 3347-3349 and 3517-3519. A scratch-validation startup failure therefore retains one-shot secrets indefinitely, contradicting the documented immediate-erasure guarantee.","evidenceState":"verified","files":["docs/host-run-usage.md","docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md","packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts"],"severity":"critical"},{"category":"missing","desc":"doc-code-drift: docs/host-run-usage.md:251-258 says a managed-review pass requires a non-empty note and rejects whitespace-only notes, matching first-stage adapter validation in packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts:1016-1019. Persistence later rejects every trimmed pass note shorter than 10 characters at packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts:3082-3088. A schema-valid 1-9-character pass note therefore fails after adapter acceptance; either the documentation and provider schema must state the 10-character minimum or persistence must accept every non-empty note.","evidenceState":"verified","files":["docs/host-run-usage.md","packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts","packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts"],"severity":"medium"}],"lane":"lattice-review-docs","providerAgent":"lattic